## Transcript

[00:00:03] Why is it important for Nvidia to release open models when Nvidia also sells GPUs to Frontier Labs that also release proprietary models? Why is it so important for you to keep pushing the envelope to release bigger and bigger models to train and to give away everything including the data, the training recipes, and kind of the teacher models? Why so? Tell us. >> I think that what I would say, what I've heard said a lot from from people like Jensen and Bryan Catanzaro, right? Jensen obviously leader of Nvidia, Bryan Catanzaro who heads up our research arm for Nvidia. I mean, it's integral, it's crucial to Nvidia's mission to be good at producing models because people use GPUs to make models. That's just a fact. They use them to train models, to inference with models, they use them to run their agents. And if we don't know how to build a good model, if we can't build a good model, we can't know what the best GPU is, right? We can't understand the exact best way to produce hardware. And this is a process that I think Jensen's talked a lot about up on various stages called extreme co-design, right? Where you have to kind of build the hardware with the technology at the same time. And if you just do one in a vacuum, it doesn't mean anything. And the reason we want to open it is because we think that AI is a very useful tool. And everyone should have AI and many different countries should have AI and many different organizations should have AI and they should have a blueprint we know works and is battle-tested that that you can take and you can build your own models and for your own agents. And if we're not releasing that stuff because we're doing it, so it's like if we're doing it, we may as well release it. Share the learnings and I think, you know, Bryan says this a lot like the ecosystem benefits when we release something because then the ecosystem does something with with our stuff and we learn from it and then we get better and then we make better hardware and then we make better models. That's just summarize the thoughts of people that are at the helm. That's why we do it. >> [music]

